+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describe a type alias at module level or in a class. The directive supports
+   description body content, but aliases cannot contain nested Python objects.
+   For example::
+
+      .. py:type:: UserId
+         :canonical: int
+
+         Identifier assigned to a user.
+
+   The optional :rst:dir:option:`canonical` option describes the represented
+   type. Its expression is shown after the alias name with an equals sign and
+   is parsed as a Python annotation, so referenced types can be cross-referenced.
+   When supplied, the expression is also registered as an alias target for the
+   documented type alias. The expression may be omitted when it is unknown or
+   not useful to display.
+
